    "result_text": "The full suite is green (70 tests, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `Cp58Tests`.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `riskFlag` is a pure function of already-derived owner state, so I surfaced it as a read-model field (like `ownerSegment`/`locality`), rather than a stored column.\n\n1. **`RiskFlag.java`** (new helper in `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 `RiskFlag.of(owner)` returns true when any of:\n   - `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` \u2014 possible duplicate (set by `AssignPossibleDuplicate`);\n   - `isDisposableAdjacent(owner.getEmail())` \u2014 the email domain carries a known disposable provider's second-level label (`mailinator`/`tempmail`/`guerrillamail`), covering the exact blocked domain, its subdomains, and alternate TLDs (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `mail.tempmail.com`);\n   - `owner.getCapacityWarning()` \u2014 city over its soft capacity of 40 (set by `AssignCapacityWarning`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", expression = \u2026)` calling the helper, so it's populated on every `OwnerDto`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema and its `required` list, so the generated DTO always includes it.\n\nThe three risk inputs are all snapshot fields stored at creation, so deriving the flag at read time yields a value consistent with when the owner was created. For a fully-unique owner (no duplicate, no email, uncrowded city) the flag is `false`, matching the test.",
